// The lobby: the session hub alone, full screen. `zj` without arguments
// (and so the Windows Terminal profile) starts a session named lobby-<id>
// with this layout when no session is open yet.
//
// Picking something in the hub moves the client to that session and closes
// the hub's pane, which ends the lobby: it has no other pane. A lobby left
// behind anyway (its window was closed) is swept by the next pilot that
// sees a client (plugins/pilot, sweep_lobbies). q in the hub leaves Zellij.
//
// No bars: there is nothing here but the hub, which draws its own hints.
layout {
    pane borderless=true {
        plugin location="lobby"
    }
}